# Analysis artifacts contain merchant PII (names, emails, phones, addresses,
# owner names) by design. Never commit them.
#
# Leading slash matters: these are anchored to the repo root so they do NOT
# match tests/fixtures/data/, which is synthetic and IS committed for
# determinism. Git cannot re-include a path under an excluded directory, so an
# unanchored `data/` here would silently drop the fixture tree from version
# control.
# Any analysis DB at the repo root, not just the configured `coa.sqlite`. A
# schema change means ingesting into a second DB alongside the old one, and
# `/coa.sqlite*` matched only that one name — so `coa_v2.sqlite` would have been
# an untracked file full of merchant PII that `git add -A` would happily stage.
/*.sqlite*
/reports/
/data/
# The hand-maintained template -> archetype map. Templates are query text with
# the PII we managed to match masked out -- which is not the same as PII-free: a
# merchant value that never reached `pii_terms` survives into the template
# verbatim, and the operator may add unmasked rows by hand.
/archetype_groups.csv

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# CodeGraph index — machine-local, rebuilt by `codegraph init -i`
/.codegraph/
